{"full":"marioizquierdo/bettertabs","name":"bettertabs","description":"Bettertabs for Rails","category":"Other","language":"Ruby","stars":43,"forks":16,"created":"2011-03-31T16:15:11Z","updated":"2024-03-18T22:22:27Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://github.com/marioizquierdo/bettertabs","topics":[],"demo":"http://bettertabs-demo.herokuapp.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:17:54.156Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:17:54.156Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:17:54.156Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:50.912Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:17:54.156Z","stars":43,"forks":16}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["We know that splitting content into several tabs is easy, but doing it well, clean, DRY, accessible, usable, testable and fast is not so simple after all.","Bettertabs is a Rails 3.1+ Engine that includes a helper and a jquery plugin to render the needed markup and javascript for a section with tabs in a declarative way, forcing you to KISS, ensuring accessibility and usability, whether the content is loaded statically or via ajax.","Starting with branch 1.5+ Bettertabs supports Rails > 6.0."],"features":["Works with tabs for static, links or ajax loaded content","Works without javascript","It changes the URL (in HTML5 browsers, using history.replaceState()), so when you use the browser's back button, you'll land in the last selected tab, and selected tabs can be permalinked.","Declarative code, that helps you to have your view code more readable and DRY","It has some basic error handling (like for example if the ajax loaded content returns an error, it redirects to the error page)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marioizquierdo/bettertabs/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"974d10beb9233b39727122bf5e5c853c07fad594a8bfd3864b1c86570d69cb9e","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:50.910Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T16:23:40.491Z","